   `<div class="grid2"><section class="panel"><h2>Source and scope</h2><dl class="source-detail"><dt>Source file</dt><dd>${esc(meta.sourceFile)}</dd><dt>Source snapshot</dt><dd>${dt(meta.snapshot)}</dd><dt>Planning date</dt><dd>${dt(state.asof)}</dd><dt>Included source sheets</dt><dd>sw-details and hw-details</dd><dt>Active records</dt><dd>${records.filter(r=>r.sheet==='sw-details').length} software/cloud; ${records.filter(r=>r.sheet==='hw-details').length} hardware</dd><dt>Source preparation</dt><dd>${esc(meta.cleansing||'Inactive rows and rows ending before the EIX export date are always removed from software and hardware before customer-specific rules. Unsupported perpetual licences are outside scope.')}</dd><dt>Consumption data</dt><dd>Usage and consumption are not inferred from entitlements.</dd></dl><p class="small muted">All Source data line references point to rows in the named source workbook, not to the pre-cleansing export. The Active-only scope describes the supported/subscribed population in this extract. Unsupported licence ownership is outside this draft.</p></section>
   <section class="panel"><h2>Currency reporting</h2><p class="small muted section-gap">${esc(basis())}</p><div class="definition"><h3>Source — Source data USD</h3><p>Software purchase: AK. Annual software support and subscriptions: AO. Hardware support: BD. ${esc(hardwareAnnualRule)} These are explicit USD columns in the source.</p></div><div class="definition"><h3>Converted — reporting currency</h3><p>Converted amounts in a non-USD reporting view use the Source data USD equivalent and the selected rate. Hardware investment applies the shared purchase-currency rule, then converts into report currency using the configurable rate table. The rate and date are included in drilldowns and exports. Default rates come from the supplied EIX Currency ratios sheet, inverted to units per 1 USD. They are editable reference ratios; their actual market observation date is not supplied. The initial reference date is the EIX snapshot date.</p></div><div class="definition"><h3>Original currency — source record</h3><p>Software local purchase (AL/AQ) and annual support (AP/AR) are retained for reference. Availability of cloud local-currency amounts depends on the source line. Hardware License Value (AD) is a one-time acquisition. Its currency always prefers same-row support currency and falls back to recorded order currency. Blank hardware acquisitions calculate as zero under the shared policy. Original order currency (BK) is preserved for review. The hardware investment KPI converts those original amounts using the editable FX table; converted totals are not USD equivalents supplied by Source data. It is separate from software acquisition totals.</p></div></section></div>
   <section class="panel"><h2>Refresh from the source workbook</h2><p class="small muted section-gap">Load a Source-data-format .xlsx file containing both detail sheets, with the documented column layout. All rows are re-read, Active status is re-applied, and every dashboard view recalculates. Processing stays in this browser.</p><div class="file-load section-gap"><label>Source snapshot date<input id="source-snapshot" type="date" value="${meta.snapshot}"></label><label>Workbook<input id="source-file" type="file" accept=".xlsx"></label><button class="primary" id="load-source">Load workbook</button></div><div id="load-status" class="status-message" role="status"></div><p class="small muted section-gap">Use Save report to preserve refreshed data and the selected reporting rate in a new HTML copy. Export selected evidence produces the current filtered records. The source workbook remains a separate file and is not changed by the dashboard. Reopen this report to restore its last saved snapshot.</p></section>
   <div class="grid2 section-gap"><section class="panel"><h2>Records requiring review</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Reason</th><th>Active source lines</th></tr></thead><tbody>${flags.map(flag=>`<tr><td><button class="link" ${attr('flag',flag)}>${esc(flag)}</button></td><td class="num">${records.filter(r=>r.flags.includes(flag)).length}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="small muted section-gap">Review counts cover the complete source population. No suspected duplicates have been removed. A single record can have several review flags.</p></section>
   <section class="panel"><h2>Additional evidence needed</h2><div class="definition"><h3>OCI consumption</h3><p>Monthly usage, currency, subscription/tenancy identifiers, allocations, top-ups and remaining balance. Match the current credit period before calculating utilization or exhaustion.</p></div><div class="definition"><h3>SaaS usage</h3><p>Subscription, product, environment, period and measured usage with its definition. Compare with the same purchased metric.</p></div><div class="definition"><h3>Financial and contract definitions</h3><p>Hardware purchase amounts and currency preference, ${esc(customerLabel)} entity scope, subscription version overlaps, renewal quotes, notice dates and contract owners.</p></div></section></div>
   <section class="panel section-gap"><h2>Export, print and save ${info('sharing')}</h2><div class="definition"><h3>Export selected evidence — CSV</h3><p>Downloads the source lines behind the current filtered page for analysis in Excel. It is not the visual dashboard. Recent Purchases applies its date window. On this source-wide reference page, use Export entity list (CSV) for the directory and its local scope/search selection.</p></div><div class="definition"><h3>Print / Save PDF — current page</h3><p>Opens the browser print dialog. Print the current report section or choose Save as PDF for a static copy. Current filters and expanded detail determine the visible content. Other dashboard sections are not automatically included; PDF does not retain interactive drilldowns.</p></div><div class="definition"><h3>Save report — complete interactive HTML</h3><p>Downloads a new HTML copy with the complete current embedded extract, current exchange rates and report settings. This is not a filtered data export: recipients can access all embedded records. ${esc(embeddedScopeNote())} It neither updates the original Excel files nor synchronizes automatically with OneDrive. Share only with authorized recipients.</p></div></section>
   <section class="panel section-gap"><h2>Interpretation references</h2><p class="small">${esc(customerLabel)} presentation. ${esc(hardwareAnnualRule)}</p><p class="small muted">Product explanations are general context; Source data provides the report values.</p><p class="small section-gap"><a href="https://www.oracle.com/cloud/universal-credits/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oracle Universal Credits</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/engineered-systems/exadata/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oracle Exadata</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/engineered-systems/zero-data-loss-recovery-appliance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oracle Recovery Appliance</a></p></section>`;
